A + B means ‘B is the daughter of A’;

A - B means ‘B is the sister of A’;

A × B means ‘B is the husband of A’;

A ÷ B means ‘A is the father of B’

If, P ÷ R × T + Q - S × U + Z, Then how is R related to Z?

questions.solution:
The pattern followed here is,

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/2e1a2f0dc142ecfb544963c2209981c3e759d0cf81e91577dd86d50c0a2dc835.png] 

The above values are positional values of vowels in the English alphabetical series.

The vowels as per the English alphabetical series are A, E, I, O, and U.

The positional values of the A, E, I, O, and U are,

A → 1;

E → 5;

I → 9;

**O → 15**;

U → 21

Hence, 15 is the correct answer.

